Inference image: make the apt Python version a build arg

Upstream's apps/inference/Dockerfile installs python3.10 from apt in its
base-cuda stage, but apps/inference/pyproject.toml requires Python
>=3.11,<3.14, so `poetry install` refuses on every cuda build at pin
e5488b2a: "The currently activated Python version 3.10.12 is not
supported by the project" (KB-76). This adds PYTHON_VERSION, defaulting
to upstream's 3.10 so nothing changes when it is unset, and clears
noble's EXTERNALLY-MANAGED marker in the same RUN (a no-op where the
file is absent). docker/interp/neuronpedia.override.yaml passes 3.12
with an Ubuntu 24.04 CUDA base, where apt carries that interpreter.

Upstream tracking: not yet filed. Delete this patch at the pin bump
that carries an upstream fix for the inference image's interpreter.

diff --git a/apps/inference/Dockerfile b/apps/inference/Dockerfile
index f6e5abf..1cfe4aa 100644
--- a/apps/inference/Dockerfile
+++ b/apps/inference/Dockerfile
@@ -70,12 +70,16 @@ ENV GIT_SSL_CAINFO=${CUSTOM_CA_BUNDLE:+/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt}
 RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
     nvidia-container-toolkit \
     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
+# Interpreter to install; the project requires >=3.11, so a base whose apt carries it
+# (Ubuntu 24.04: python3.12) needs this set. Unset, the upstream value is used.
+ARG PYTHON_VERSION=3.10
 RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
-    python3.10 \
+    python${PYTHON_VERSION} \
     python3-pip \
-    python3.10-venv \
+    python${PYTHON_VERSION}-venv \
     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
-    && ln -s /usr/bin/python3.10 /usr/bin/python
+    && ln -s /usr/bin/python${PYTHON_VERSION} /usr/bin/python \
+    && rm -f /usr/lib/python${PYTHON_VERSION}/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED
 
 # Main build stage
 FROM base-${BUILD_TYPE:-nocuda} AS final
